Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["READ ME", "Chapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8217793436353235`*^9, 
  3.8217793565457916`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"431d1280-71e3-4c00-9df7-\
729a12e9b744"],

Cell["\<\
In order for this notebook to evaluate properly, please download the packages \
specified in the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Load Packages\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
section.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8217793713222775`*^9, 3.8217794255851355`*^9}, {
  3.821954270234766*^9, 
  3.821954279582634*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f2a77edf-3b7d-4591-bba3-\
5de8e1aa193c"],

Cell["\<\
We begin by giving a quick run through on how to generate vacuum characters \
of certain VOAs with this code. We will also give advice on how to generalise \
the code to other VOAs after some sample calculations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8217794596230946`*^9, 3.8217795062882824`*^9}, {
  3.821779548068535*^9, 3.821779675919578*^9}, {3.821954287840537*^9, 
  3.82195430668507*^9}, {3.8219543435519047`*^9, 
  3.821954352156411*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"20fa23c1-2e6a-4073-b691-\
97b24183bf97"],

Cell["\<\
NOTE: We recommend restarting the kernel when swapping between different VOA \
calculations. This is due to the fact that the codes share definitions of \
variables which may cause errors.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8217892450725307`*^9, 
  3.821789318204728*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"849cca36-0cea-415f-80c7-\
2c7705a7e5d0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["User Guide", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8217797045499997`*^9, 3.8217797074283037`*^9}, {
  3.821954361326026*^9, 
  3.821954361426202*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"585c95ce-02b7-4844-abc0-\
bff03d5675e7"],

Cell["\<\
Here we give a list of steps and some examples on how to run the code.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.821779834244115*^9, 3.821779874558287*^9}, {
  3.82195437491604*^9, 
  3.821954393713895*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5b930ac3-0ecc-4ec3-b656-\
91ce36b9db12"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["1.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Open the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Load Packages\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
chapter and make sure that the package requirements listed within are loaded \
correctly by Mathematica. We included a set directory command just in case \
the packages need to be navigated to. \n\nNOTE: The first package should be \
downloaded and saved as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]ope.math\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] but called with \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]<<ope.math.m\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] as seen below.\n\nThis is what it should look like \
when they are loaded correctly:"
}], "Text",
