  3.821954638086821*^9}, {3.8219623925477037`*^9, 3.821962432326442*^9}, {
  3.821962462870454*^9, 
  3.821962484572588*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"69284abb-39ea-43dd-984a-\
b70e0955ebc2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["3.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Pick a specific VOA. There are 4 copies of very similar code in this \
notebook; everything which will be said from here on is relevant for all \
cases. \n\nExpand the title related to the relevant VOA and run the entirety \
of the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Definitions\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section. \
This will define the variables used for the OPEs (bosonic and fermionic), as \
well as the definitions of the abstract VOA generators in terms of the \
\[Beta]\[Gamma]bc system. There is no user input required at this point."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8217872833914943`*^9, 3.821787450592868*^9}, {
  3.821953147145849*^9, 3.8219531874990177`*^9}, {3.8219546417098417`*^9, 
  3.821954693482435*^9}, {3.821954728210762*^9, 
  3.821954729650544*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cd77cf2e-3eee-4ca5-9791-\
70bdda2a2629"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["4.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Open the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Character Calculation\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] chapter and run the entirety of the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Field Generation\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section. This \
will generate all possible configurations built out of the strong generators \
and their derivatives (given in the earlier sections in terms of free fields) \
at the specific weight specified by the user in lev. No user input is \
required at this stage."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.821780904557022*^9, 3.821780905082616*^9}, {
  3.821780952647397*^9, 3.8217809848093743`*^9}, {3.821781021319721*^9, 
  3.8217810643047523`*^9}, {3.821787472127922*^9, 3.821787477129664*^9}, {
  3.821954744141746*^9, 3.8219547648186817`*^9}, {3.821962504260295*^9, 
  3.821962512122882*^9}, {3.821962568700006*^9, 
  3.8219626387535877`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7c6b4557-781c-4241-80c0-\
cd7b7c36e5c7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["5.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Run the entirety of the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Selection via Quantum \
Numbers\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section. This section of the code grades the \
previously generated operators by the symmetries of the N=2 VOA. No user \
input is required at this stage."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8217809909290075`*^9, 3.821781010270275*^9}, {
  3.821781072443982*^9, 3.8217811637427893`*^9}, {3.8217828118688574`*^9, 
  3.8217828160536623`*^9}, {3.8217874704388723`*^9, 3.821787481475789*^9}, {
  3.821954796094554*^9, 
  3.821954802944553*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"198cc6e9-dbf0-4a20-ab19-\
b3ae2f496278"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["6.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Run the entirety of the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Pre-Processing\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section. No user input is required at this stage."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8217809909290075`*^9, 3.821781010270275*^9}, {
   3.8217811277969327`*^9, 3.8217811321662493`*^9}, {3.8217811695921445`*^9, 
   3.821781169893339*^9}, 3.821782823868759*^9, {3.8218764113938894`*^9, 
   3.8218764114686823`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"28b1eb1c-490a-4b80-a916-\
a022e3f74b15"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["7.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Choose whether to run the most refined calculation, or save computational \
power and do an unrefined calculation. The former includes an R-filtration \
grading, while the latter one does not. The codes for calculating both are \
given in the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Calculating Physical States\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section, given by \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]R-Filtration Level-by-Level Character Calculator\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Level-by-Level Character \
Calculator\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] subsections respectively. Evaluating the \
required subsubsection computes the vacuum character at the requested level.\n\
\nNOTE: At this stage the code determines the degeneracy of null states for \
fixed quantum numbers. The result is then subtracted from the naive \
degeneracy of states."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.821781200859515*^9, 3.821781481336336*^9}, {
   3.821782842911826*^9, 3.821782851329311*^9}, {3.821876413134794*^9, 
   3.8218764132375183`*^9}, {3.8218817938181257`*^9, 3.821881919886895*^9}, {
