Cell["\<\
NOTE: If the fcal option was selected, the above degeneracies will only \
include non-negatively charged states (under the red gl(1) symmetry). This \
result shows the list of all the states along with their degeneracies and all \
the quantum numbers. The bold number is the degeneracy; inside the square \
brackets are the quantum numbers: red is for m (gl(1) in osp(2|2)), while \
blue is for r (gl(1) outer automorphism).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8217816544895787`*^9, 3.8217817520943856`*^9}, {
   3.821781783277981*^9, 3.8217818792632647`*^9}, {3.8218819460409346`*^9, 
   3.821881947658606*^9}, {3.8219539017291327`*^9, 3.8219539190763474`*^9}, {
   3.821955091969084*^9, 3.8219551497039213`*^9}, 3.821963486488226*^9, {
   3.8219645208383017`*^9, 3.821964521331915*^9}, {3.821972412005067*^9, 
   3.821972432076809*^9}, 
   3.82284825250922*^9},ExpressionUUID->"9e757e78-d068-4cbd-bc87-\
2196346c5263"],

