Cell["\<\
In this section we define all the operators being used in our code. Both the \
free fields (b, c, \[Beta], \[Gamma]) and the abstract algebra strong \
generators. (In order to generalise the code to higher ranks or other \
algebras, one must change and/or add the generators appearing in the new \
algebra in the definitions below. We will highlight where change is needed \
throughout the code with comments CNH = Change Needed Here. The comment \
should be understood for multiple lines. There is more information about this \
under the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]READ ME//Advice on Generalisation\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] section.)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.816929667468338*^9, 3.816929708804813*^9}, {
